  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 04d79210d2564f739f9a05a738b8a1d3, type: 3}
  m_Name: ReadMe
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: EasyIdleGame::EasyIdleGame.Demos.DemoSceneReadme
  data:
    title: Production Modifiers
    summary: A scene-level production modifier adds bonus Coins based on owned factory
      copies. The factory itself has a fixed output table, making the modifier's effect
      easy to compare in round, per-second, active, and offline calculations.
    resourcePrefix: demo_prodmod
    sections:
    - heading: Project setup
      body: Add a ProductionModifierManager to the scene manager GameObject and assign
        modifier assets to its list. The manager registers them while it is enabled
        and unregisters them when disabled, so stale static registrations cannot leak
        into other scenes.
    - heading: What to try
      body: Start with the modifier enabled. Twelve factories produce 96 base Coins
        per round (12 x 8), while floor(12 / 3) x 25 adds 100 bonus Coins, for 196
        total or 49 Coins/second over the four-second round. Disable the bonus to
        see the fixed base remain at 96 Coins/round and 24 Coins/second. Press Start
        all to populate the current-active rate, use Buy +3 to reach 15 factories,
        then use the pre-granted Offline automation boost before comparing offline
        profit with the modifier enabled and disabled. The factory remains manual
        until that temporary boost is activated.
    - heading: Caveats
      body: The Business asset does not scale itself; the ProductionModifierManager
        owns registration for the separate modifier asset. Modifiers receive calculated
        output lists and must not mutate shared output assets. Order matters when several
        modifiers change the same output; lower priority runs earlier. The built-in
        modifier can target currency, business, boost, or manager output. Offline
        profit includes only businesses currently eligible for automatic production;
        this demo supplies that eligibility with a temporary boost instead of enabling
        Auto Produce on the Business asset.
